    "result_text": "All 261 tests pass. The redesign is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, and cascaded that change to every value derived from it.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 rewritten to build `customerCode` as:\n- **REGION**: the region code derived from the postcode (preferred), falling back to the city, then `UNKNOWN` \u2014 reusing the existing region/postcode tables.\n- **HASH8**: the first 8 upper-case hex characters of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`. The telephone is already canonical E.164 at this point (`NormalizeOwnerTelephone` runs earlier in the pipeline).\n- Dropped the per-city sequence entirely, so the `OwnerRepository` dependency and `findAll()` scan are gone.\n\nEverything downstream reads `customerCode`, so it flowed through automatically, with docs updated to match:\n- **`AssignMembershipNumber`** \u2014 still `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, now producing e.g. `NSW-1A2B3C4D-M26`.\n- **`OwnerMapper.checkDigit`** \u2014 the Luhn check digit now runs over the digits in the new code (hex digits of the hash; region/letters/hyphen skipped).\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 the create audit line now logs the new code (confirmed in test output: `owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E ...`).\n- **`OwnerMapper.locality`** \u2014 moved onto the identity: it now reads the REGION prefix out of `customerCode`, keeping locality and identity in lock-step. Owners with no `customerCode` (seed data) fall back to the historical postcode/city derivation, so existing reads don't regress.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` passes (code matches `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`), as do all 28 owner controller tests and the full 261-test suite.",
